--- !u!114 &8005371196247960192
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Let's now switch the Exposure Mode to another one that can automatically adapt to the Scene's lighting.\n\n1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> select the <b>Global Volume</b> created at the previous step.\n\n2. In its <i>Inspector,</i> Switch the Mode to <b>Automatic Histogram.</b>\n\nExplore the Scene and notice how the camera now imitates the human eye adaptation or the automatic exposure system of a camera. Dark areas may become brighter, and bright ones may turn darker, automatically.\n\n\n<b>Expert tips</b>\n\n\u2022 Use the <b>Limit Min</b> and <b>Limit Max</b> overrides to control how much the Automatic Exposure can fluctuate within a fixed range of values, to prevent it from displaying too dark or too bright images.\n\n\u2022 Use the <b>Compensation</b> overrie to slightly nudge the exposure up or down in case you aren't exactly satisfied with the exposure value selected by the system.\n\n\u2022 HDRP offers a wide range of mid grey targets, from 12.5% to 18% grey, to simulate the exposure system from most camera manufacturers."
--- !u!114 &8380277224152115777
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this tutorial, you learned how to control the exposure to adjust the perceived brightness of a Scene.\r\n\r\nWhile exposure is a complex topic, understanding it can help you greatly improve the visual quality of your projects.\r\n\r\nFor more information about Exposure, watch this  in-depth <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yqCHiZrgKzs?t=1026\">video tutorial.</a>\r\n\r\nYou can also learn more about exposure and how to debug it in the <a href=\"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.high-definition@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/Override-Exposure.html\">documentation.</a>\r\n\r\n<b>Note:</b> You do not need to save your changes in order to follow other tutorials.\r"
